#: ../../source/components_basic/10-component_soil.rst:95
msgid "In this part of the code, a constant integer named sensorPin is defined and assigned the value A0. A0 is the analog input pin on the Arduino board where the soil moisture sensor is connected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/10-component_soil.rst:101
msgid "Setting up the serial communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/10-component_soil.rst:103
msgid "The ``setup()`` function is called once when the Arduino is powered on or reset. Here, we initialize the Serial library at 9600 baud rate. The baud rate is the rate at which information is transferred. In this case, it's 9600 bits per second (bps)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/10-component_soil.rst:111
msgid "Reading data and printing to the serial monitor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/10-component_soil.rst:113
msgid "The loop function is where the main logic of the program resides. This function loops indefinitely once the program starts. Inside the loop, we use the ``analogRead()`` function to read the data from the moisture sensor and print it to the Serial Monitor. We then pause the program for 500 milliseconds using the delay function before taking the next reading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/10-component_soil.rst:124
msgid "The smaller the value, the higher the soil moisture level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/10-component_soil.rst:127
msgid "Additional Ideas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/10-component_soil.rst:129
msgid "Integrate a buzzer or LED that activates if the moisture level goes below a certain threshold. This way, you'll have a physical alert to water your plants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/10-component_soil.rst:130
msgid "You could connect a water pump and automate the watering process. When the moisture level drops below a threshold, the Arduino can activate the pump to water the plants."
msgstr ""

